{"name":"Ionian","hex":"#368976","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ionian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to the Hellenic people of that name.","Synonym of Ionic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Ionians, one of the races of Ancient Greece."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ionian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ionian mode","blocks":[{"text":"The Ionian mode is a musical mode or, in modern usage, a diatonic scale also called the major scale. It is named after the Ionian Greeks."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionian_mode","wikidata":"Q1167788"},{"title":"Ionian Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Ionian Sea is an elongated bay of the Mediterranean Sea. It is connected to the Adriatic Sea to the north, and is bounded by Southern Italy, including Basilicata, Calabria, Sicily, and the Salento peninsula to the west, southern Albania to the north, and the west coast of Greece, including the Peloponnese."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ionian_Sea_borders.png/330px-Ionian_Sea_borders.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionian_Sea","wikidata":"Q37495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ionian_Sea_borders.png/500px-Ionian_Sea_borders.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ionian_Sea_borders.png/500px-Ionian_Sea_borders.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIonian_Sea_borders.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Kipouria1.JPG/500px-Kipouria1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Kipouria1.JPG/1280px-Kipouria1.JPG?utm_source